            <title>[LU-20954] build: configure fails on kernel without InfiniBand by default</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20954</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;Claude&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; Building Lustre against a kernel without InfiniBand (CONFIG_INFINIBAND not set, e.g. many aarch64 VM kernels) fails at configure unless &lt;tt&gt;--with-o2ib=no&lt;/tt&gt; is given:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;configure: error: cannot compile with OpenIB gen2 headers
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In &lt;tt&gt;config/lustre-lnet.m4&lt;/tt&gt; the &lt;tt&gt;-&lt;del&gt;with-o2ib&lt;/tt&gt; default is &lt;tt&gt;with_o2ib="yes"&lt;/tt&gt;, so the default cannot be told apart from an explicit &lt;tt&gt;&lt;/del&gt;-with-o2ib=yes&lt;/tt&gt;.  The in-kernel o2ib check only tests that &lt;tt&gt;rdma/rdma_cm.h&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;rdma/ib_cm.h&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;rdma/ib_verbs.h&lt;/tt&gt; exist, and those headers are present in every kernel tree whether or not IB is configured.  The following "OpenIB gen2 support" compile test then fails on &lt;tt&gt;rdma_destroy_id()&lt;/tt&gt;, and because &lt;tt&gt;ENABLEO2IB="yes"&lt;/tt&gt; it is a hard error rather than disabling o2iblnd.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Proposed fix:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;make the default auto-detect, separate from an explicit &lt;tt&gt;--with-o2ib=yes&lt;/tt&gt;;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;only consider in-kernel o2iblnd buildable if the kernel has &lt;tt&gt;CONFIG_INFINIBAND&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;CONFIG_INFINIBAND_ADDR_TRANS&lt;/tt&gt; (rdma_cm), otherwise warn and build without it, as already done when the headers are missing;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;keep the hard error for an explicit &lt;tt&gt;-&lt;del&gt;with-o2ib=yes&lt;/tt&gt; or &lt;tt&gt;&lt;/del&gt;-with-o2ib=&amp;lt;path&amp;gt;&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Seen with ltvm, which now passes &lt;tt&gt;--with-o2ib=yes&lt;/tt&gt; by default (lustre-test-vms PR #29), on rocky8/9/10 and Ubuntu 26.04 aarch64 kernels.  Related: patch &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/69451" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/69451&lt;/a&gt; ("&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20872" title="build: packaging doesn't honor o2ib configuration from configure" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20872"&gt;LU-20872&lt;/a&gt; build: Honor o2ib configuration in packaging") also changes the o2ib detection.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
